      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "take this to be equivalent to तथापि. तत्क्षणभङ्गि.—स एव क्षणः तत्क्षणः",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "the moment a man becomes a Purusharatna; तस्मिन् भज्यते",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "इत्येवंशीलम् ।",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 96. नायकोप्योव०-ओषः ( fr. उष् to burn ) पाको धीयते अत्र इति",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "ओषधिः। A plant, a medicinal drug.; also an herb which dies when",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "its fruit becomes ripe. The moon is often called the Lord of",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "herbs, probably because plants thrive under the influenc of",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "moon-light. Cf. Rg. X. 85.—सोमेनादित्या बलिनः सोमेन पृथिवी",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "मही ।' where Sáyana says—अमृतसेकेनौषध्यभिवृद्ध्या पृथिव्या बलवत्त्वम् ।",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "‘ ततस्तस्मै ददौ राज्यं ब्रह्मा ब्रह्मविदां वरः । बीजौषधीनां विप्राणामपां च",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "जनमेजय ’ ॥ Hv. XXV. See also Váy. P. XXVIII. 12. 16. Mat.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "P. XXIII. 10–13. More probably, however, ओषधीनाथ is Soma,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 12,
          "text": "the plant, the juice of which formed the well known beverage",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 13,
          "text": "of the ancient Rishis. By a curious misapplication of names",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 14,
          "text": "the term Soma came to be an appellation of the moon and so all",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 15,
          "text": "the epithets of Soma, the plant, were transferred to Soma, the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 16,
          "text": "moon. See notes on Rag. II. 73. भिषक्–बिभेत्यस्माद्रोगः a physi-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 17,
          "text": "cian. शतभिषक्—(1) a hundred physicians; (2) name of the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 18,
          "text": "24th lunar mansion ( the S'atatárakàs ) containing one huudred",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 19,
          "text": "stars. अवतंस—an ear-ring or an ornament worn on the head.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 20,
          "text": "All these adjectives indicate that the moon had the means to",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 21,
          "text": "counteract the effects of the disease. राजयक्ष्मा—consumption",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 22,
          "text": "which attacked the moon; also consumption in general. So",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 23,
          "text": "called because it is, as it were, the prince of diseases ( यक्ष्मणां",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 24,
          "text": "रोगाणां राजा ). Cf. राजयक्ष्मेव रोगाणां समूहः स महीभृताम् S'is. II.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 25,
          "text": "96, commenting on which Malli. quotes from Vàgbhatta—",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 26,
          "text": "अनेकरोगानु० ( see com. )—शोषो रोगराडिति च स्मृतः ॥ नक्षत्राणां द्विजानां",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 27,
          "text": "च राज्ञोऽभूद्यदयं पुरा । यच्च राजा च यक्ष्मा च राजयक्ष्मा ततो मतः ॥ The moon",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 28,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 29,
          "text": "was cursed to be eternally consumptive by his father-in-law,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 30,
          "text": "Daksha, for paying sole attention to Rohini and neglecting his",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 31,
          "text": "other daughters. At the intercession of his wives the sentence",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 32,
          "text": "of eternal consumption was commuted to one of periodical",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 33,
          "text": "consumption.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 97. प्रभुणा—प्रभवतीति प्रभुः, used in a literal sense, power-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "ful, having power to dispense. प्रमाणीकृतं-प्राप्यत्वेन निर्णीतम् Ráma",
          "end": "join"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "",
          "end": "join"
